text='''# OpenCorvus L06/0.3 candidate: independent content and science review

The five frozen content leaves **H01–H05 are verified_pass**, bound to assignment `l06-whole-fcfd7bffdb9e4b97b27a99389fc365d0`, case `L06/0.3.0-dev`. No machine leaf or aggregate score was authored. The actual grader remains the root's responsibility.

I read this candidate's own REPORT/HANDOFF/actor/model/output/source map, original private native records and both actual PNGs. I did not substitute author or Codex prose/ratings. No new candidate, native exercise, cold run, optimizer, LP, test, grader, Provider, Task/service, Docker/WSL, UI, GPU or L01 operation occurred. New calculations were standard-library raw CSV/Fraction/SQLite/ZIP audits; all SQLite originals and existing WAL/SHM were first copied into this review's own directory before opening, avoiding read-only-connection sidecar writes to originals.

## Substantive result

Independent arithmetic closes all128private business weeks, strict action tensors/complete observed histories, complete current packets/responses, original SQL event/action/receipt and derived states/queues. There are60full-history decision nodes. All declared2944action CSV coordinates and128weekly monetary/peak rows agree, including zeros. Expected cost is197049/4=49262.25 with purchase292949/8, freight12615/2, production5802 and holding4273/8. I separately construct the specified canonical current-needs spot algorithm from original tables, obtaining70640 and saving85511/4. This is a physical/causal comparison, not adoption of a weak candidate baseline.

Minimum settled cash is−3298 on every path. Final cash ranges from35269 to37386, all nonnegative. Final AR24150 on even paths or25230 on odd paths is exactly due16..19; none is spent early. Maximum raw peak239 and finished peak87 remain within240/100. The original eight private paths perform128commits and one controller73→0original8-row receipt recovery; the separate reordered input control commits16with the same actual path business record. Native private batch6.6159257seconds is execution evidence, not candidate useful hours.

Model source shares full-history nodes and ancestor orders in the causal mixed-integer case. Its separate perfect-information branch removes sharing and integrality while retaining the physical/timing model. The candidate honestly labels time-limited causal status1, dual47658.125 and gap as numerical diagnostics. Continuous46727.84821428571/status0 is explicitly non-deployable and not a perfect-information integer optimum or independently replayed rational certificate. I did not solve either model again. The weaker39714 analytical relaxation is independently proved/calculated from horizon production needs, initial raw offsets, cheapest quoted unit/allowed-route costs and nonnegative waived freight/holding. Neither that loose bound nor the feasible incumbent proves global optimum.

The handoff gives usable native paths/commands, scientific dependency separation, same-key original receipt recovery, WAL-aware preservation, immutable commitments and named stop/replan/authorized-credit decisions. It warns against mixing old journals with a newly solved policy or asserting spot as an automatic mid-policy rescue. Source archive bytes match complete delivered files, and original native argv actually consume the sealed actor. Actual scientific package metadata match its local declared lock; no installation was performed here.

Both supplied images were actually opened. Cash/storage has path/unit/week labels and both cash floors/stage limits. Component/path costs match independently recomputed values. The expected continuous-relaxation line is explicitly labelled as expected, not a per-path lower bound; report cautions about deployability and finite scope. Markdown and actual PNGs are the reviewed usable report; I did not claim an independent PDF-render pass.

## Preserved failures and evidence limits

The candidate's deliberately forged packet has retained raw stderr and native exit1. Its own separate internal review reports an initial state-export mismatch from retained consumed queue entries and documents its correction, plus newly created empty WAL/SHM sidecars and narrowly removing those reviewer-created files. These structured records also exist unchanged inside its review evidence ZIP. I independently checked current original and internal-review actual SQL states against my own recurrence rather than accepting their PASS/verdict. I did not call Task/service to fetch the cited initial Host tool part; that first-checker history remains a disclosed structured record, not a newly verified raw terminal trace. The internal review's “Accepted” is not this external review's authority.

My own provenance audit initially used an incorrect sibling `X/public` locator, which is absent in this occurrence, so only the public-identity check returnedfalse and tool exit1. The actual original inputs are `X/project/public`. I preserved that script/result, then checked only the corrected25-file original root against original workspace ZIP and closed private public, all equal. No business calculation or candidate file was changed, no native rerun occurred, and this reviewer locator error is not a candidate failure. See reviewer-public-locator-correction.json.

Original source/capsules and the layout/2 locator bind this candidate's actor/, results/, JSONsource map, HANDOFFcommands and twoimages. They are actual original workspace bytes. Layout/format neutrality was honored; no author root filename, language or figure count was imposed. All17frozen leaf definitions/weights remain unchanged. Identity establishes provenance, while the independent equations/SQL establish numerical support.

No substantive five-leaf deficiency or current wrong-object binding was observed. Root should run its actual frozen aggregate; this file supplies no score. This familiar nonblind AI review is not a professional-human/statistical maturity, real financial approval, arbitrary-failure, effective-hour or ten-task completion certification, nor a matched-model ranking against Codex. Any new difficulty/version decision must preserve this frozen candidate's original result.
'''
